--- desc: B-729 — instance method with non-fn body emits lower-warning
[
  # Define a simple class
  Monoid: [class [let a]]

  # Define a function that will be used as a method
  my-add: [fn [let a@Int b@Int] [+ a b]]

  # Instance with non-fn body — should emit warning
  MonoidInt: [instance Monoid [let a@Int]: [append: my-add]]

  # Use the instance
  result: [MonoidInt.append 3 4]
]
=== out
[0: [
  Monoid: <class Monoid>
  my-add: <fn>
  MonoidInt: [append: <fn>]
  result: 7
]]
=== warn
instance method 'append': non-fn body cannot carry instance_of stamp — use an explicit [fn ...] wrapper
